DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions are used to access or to change the NIS domain name of
       the host system.  More precisely, they operate on the NIS  domain  name
       associated with the calling process’s UTS namespace.

       sseettddoommaaiinnnnaammee()  sets the domain name to the value given in the charac‐
       ter array _n_a_m_e.  The _s_i_z_e argument specifies the  number  of  bytes  in
       _n_a_m_e.  (Thus, _n_a_m_e does not require a terminating null byte.)

       ggeettddoommaaiinnnnaammee()  returns the null‐terminated domain name in the charac‐
       ter array _n_a_m_e, which has a size of _s_i_z_e bytes.  If the null‐terminated
       domain name requires more than _l_e_n bytes, ggeettddoommaaiinnnnaammee()  returns  the
       first _l_e_n bytes (glibc) or gives an error (libc).

